WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.480
128 billion dollars in crown assets are set to merge to grow Canadian firms abroad. This is Omni

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:13.400
View North America, episode 45. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host, a September 11th

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:18.240
trial date, a ticket contract at the Kennedy Center, and a Canadian turn back to old gadgets

00:00:18.240 --> 00:00:24.160
come next. Then who gets to refuse a landfill in Ontario? Export development Canada and the

00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:28.580
business development bank of Canada are the two crown lenders Ottawa has ordered to combine,

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:33.160
A step promised in the federal budget earlier this month, the Globe and Mail reports.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.500
Between them, they employ 5,100 people and work in more than two dozen countries.

00:00:39.140 --> 00:00:46.180
Allison Nankavell, who runs Export Development Canada, says the point is more Canadian firms large enough to operate in several markets,

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:48.540
and she says this is not a savings drive.

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:51.880
She wants a bigger balance sheet that can shift money where it is needed.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:57.060
Two people who know the plans and whom the Globe is not naming because they were not clear to speak,

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:01.340
say the merged body will answer to the finance minister inside a wider poll

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:06.160
together of federal financing agencies. A white paper EDC put out in September

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:11.480
ranked Canada 35th for how complex the goods it makes are. Behind Japan, South

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:17.640
Korea, Germany, China, Sweden, Italy, the United States and France. EDC's own

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.880
estimate is that more complex products could add $100 billion to GDP.

00:01:22.580 --> 00:01:27.880
Nankavell names critical minerals, the energy transition, artificial intelligence, agra

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:32.400
food and forestry as places to press, and she says broken trade with the United States

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:36.260
means companies can no longer treat a cross-border supply chain as automatic.

00:01:36.980 --> 00:01:42.240
Tushar Handikar, her vice president for structured and project finance, expects foreign export

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:47.000
agencies or insurers to carry part of the risk, and she expects the asset book to grow as

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:48.660
more firms are financed overseas.

00:01:49.744 --> 00:01:55.364
A judge has fixed June 5, 2028, the New York Times reports, as the trial date for four

00:01:55.364 --> 00:01:59.764
men accused of conspiring in the 2001 attacks that killed nearly 3,000 people.

00:02:00.284 --> 00:02:05.424
The time says years of United States government choices, from coerced confessions to a separate

00:02:05.424 --> 00:02:08.164
court system, wrecked any chance of a fast trial.

00:02:08.644 --> 00:02:13.364
The Kennedy Center is planning to move its tickets to ticket master, and NPR says that plan

00:02:13.364 --> 00:02:18.124
is drawing conflict of interest concerns because former President Richard Grinnell sat as a paid

00:02:18.124 --> 00:02:23.840
board member of Ticketmaster's parent while the two sides were still negotiating. Younger Canadians

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:29.040
are buying the gadgets their parents boxed up. Global news reports from a Best Buy Canada survey run

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:34.100
by Angus Reed. 40 percent of Canadians say they are likely to buy a holiday gift out of nostalgia,

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:40.480
and that share is 53 percent among millennials and 49 percent among Gen Z. Kushal Sami,

00:02:40.480 --> 00:02:47.540
Best Buy Canada's director of brand marketing says those buyers want a device that feels personal, not a costume of the past.

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:53.640
A third of people in the survey want old tech because they like owning the physical thing, a record or a game cartridge.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.580
23% bought music, movies or games in a physical format in the last year.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:03.580
32% of millennials, 30% of Gen Z, and 12% of boomers.

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:07.140
Gen Z leans toward the Apple iPod, then the Blackberry.

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:11.480
Millenials want consoles such as the Nintendo 64 or the Super Nintendo.

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:14.040
Boomers miss VCRs in VHS.

00:03:14.700 --> 00:03:19.820
Another Angus Reed survey out last month found 37% of Canadians had dropped at least one

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:23.900
streaming service in six months, up from 32% four years earlier.

00:03:24.480 --> 00:03:29.840
Best Buy says headphones, earbuds, consoles, and turn tables are busy categories this season.

00:03:30.858 --> 00:03:35.298
In the rest of the day's news, Senator Cindy Hyde Smith conceded Wednesday to Democrat

00:03:35.298 --> 00:03:42.338
Scott Colum, who took 49.2% to her 48.7%, fewer than 5,000 votes out of nearly a million,

00:03:42.818 --> 00:03:48.058
leaving Democrats with 55 Senate seats and Alaska still uncalled. And she said she respected

00:03:48.058 --> 00:03:53.118
Mississippi voters even though it was not the result she wanted. San Antonio is suing to stop

00:03:53.118 --> 00:03:58.018
a warehouse from becoming an ICE detention center. One case in a wider set of lawsuits

00:03:58.018 --> 00:04:01.698
slowing the Trump administration's push to build immigration detention sites.

00:04:01.698 --> 00:04:07.098
The Education Department has finished a rule that NPR links to a 2023 campaign promise

00:04:07.098 --> 00:04:11.198
by President Trump to take universities back from what he called the radical left.

00:04:11.758 --> 00:04:16.678
At least 23 states looked at laws on ICE in schools this year, while educators still

00:04:16.678 --> 00:04:18.758
work from a patchwork when agents show up.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:23.938
A Democratic leader said the Mist vote on Defense Secretary Pete Hegseth disappointed Americans.

00:04:24.638 --> 00:04:28.878
Florida Republican leaders are cool to a push by DeSantis for a property tax session.

00:04:28.878 --> 00:04:34.578
Democrats have flipped at least 27 seats in the New Hampshire legislature and on the executive council.

00:04:35.098 --> 00:04:39.998
Former Hawaii State Senate leader Brenton Awa has left the Republican Party to sit as an independent.

00:04:40.558 --> 00:04:44.838
Minnesota Republicans say they want to seat at the table under a new DFL trifecta.

00:04:45.338 --> 00:04:49.458
Three Ontario private career colleges have laid off staff during an OSAP pause,

00:04:49.778 --> 00:04:52.578
and one has stopped classes for about 300 students.

00:04:53.038 --> 00:04:57.618
Canada says Russian players who already hold visas will still be kept out of the world juniors,

00:04:57.618 --> 00:05:03.858
which looks like a closed door after last month's court ruling that the IIHF must put Russia back in international hockey.

00:05:04.378 --> 00:05:07.398
A source told CBC News that Ottawa had known for months

00:05:07.398 --> 00:05:12.358
Stellantis might sell its Brampton Ontario assembly plant to a maker of light-armored vehicles.

00:05:12.978 --> 00:05:17.558
Quebec's PQ government is preparing a bill to restrict access to English-language sea-geps.

00:05:18.138 --> 00:05:22.878
Mark Carney is set to sign two Asian trade deals on a nine-day trip that takes in four summits,

00:05:23.278 --> 00:05:26.578
a journey the Toronto Starcast says a test of his middle-power pitch.

00:05:26.578 --> 00:05:31.858
A Quebec woman with ALS can hear her own voice again through an AI app that global news

00:05:31.858 --> 00:05:33.918
says makes talk faster and more personal.

